  "result": "I added `getIssueParticipants` and its supporting schema and repository function. A `tsc --noEmit` run reported no errors in the three edited files.\n\n- **`src/schemas/comment.ts`**: `issueParticipantsSchema` (`orgId`, `issueId`) and `IssueParticipantsInput`.\n- **`src/server/repositories/comment-repository.ts`**: `listCommentAuthorIds`, which selects distinct author ids from live comments on the issue in the org.\n- **`src/server/services/comment-service.ts`**: `getIssueParticipants`, which follows the same checks as `getThread`: tenant scope, then issue lookup, then `comment:read`. It collects the issue author, the assignee, and the live comment authors into a set, then keeps only users whose membership is `active` and not archived.\n\nThe membership check calls the existing `findMember` once per candidate rather than adding a batch helper, to keep the set of new exports to the three you listed. That is N+1 queries per request; if participant lists get large, a batch member lookup would be the fix.",
